## Folder Structure

Every case folder uses these six standard subfolders. Create any that are missing; do not rename or restructure them.

| Folder | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `Email Correspondence` | All email communications related to the case — attorney-to-attorney, client communications, court notices received by email, opposing counsel correspondence |
| `Fact Research` | Client-produced documents, leases, ledgers, inspection reports, photographs, contracts, applications, payment records, and other factual evidence |
| `Legal Research` | Statutes, rules, case law, legal memoranda, and research notes |
| `Miscellaneous` | Filing templates, letterhead templates, engagement letters, billing records, and anything that doesn't fit the other categories |
| `Pleadings` | All court filings — complaints, answers, motions, oppositions, replies, orders, summons, writs. Named with sequential `PLD-###` prefix |
| `Raw Documents` | Unprocessed uploads — the original staging area. **Never delete or rename files here.** Originals stay to preserve provenance; organized copies go to the appropriate subfolder |

### Classification Rules

When filing a new document, use these rules:

- Court filings, summons, complaints, motions, orders → `Pleadings`
- Emails between attorneys, from clients, from courts, from opposing parties → `Email Correspondence`
- Leases, ledgers, applications, inspection reports, contracts, payment records, client-produced documents → `Fact Research`
- Statutes, case law, legal memos → `Legal Research`
- Engagement letters, billing, templates → `Miscellaneous`
- If a document could belong in multiple folders, copy it to all appropriate locations
- When in doubt, file to `Fact Research` and note the ambiguity in the activity log

### Pleading File Naming

All files in `Pleadings/` use this naming convention:

```
PLD-### [Document Title] ([Case Style], Filed YYYY-MM-DD).pdf
```

Example: `PLD-001 Complaint (Smith v. Jones, Filed 2026-03-15).pdf`

The complaint is always PLD-001. Continue sequential numbering from the highest existing PLD-### number.

